</form><html xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:math="java.lang.Math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions" xmlns:xdt="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-datatypes" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>SR139:v99#DOCUMENT</title><meta name="dc:identifier" content="SR139"/><meta name="dc:title" content="SR &#xA;              139-&#xA;                INTRODUCED&#xA;              "/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/></head><body><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Start</h2></span><div id="bill_all" align="justify"><div id="about"><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td align="center"/></tr></tbody></table></div><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><font size="3" style="FONT-FAMILY: MinionPC, Arial Unicode MS">
                    CALIFORNIA LEGISLATURE—
                    2025–2026 REGULAR SESSION</font></div><br clear="all"/><span id="bill_house_num"><div style="float: left; width:50%; font-weight: bold; "><span style="text-transform: uppercase; text-align:left;width:50%;"><b>
                Senate Resolution
              </b></span></div><div style="float:right; width:50%; text-align:right;"><span style="text-transform: uppercase;"><b>No. 139</b></span></div></span><hr/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td id="bill_authors" align="center"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Introduced by Senator Becker<br/></span></td></tr><tr><td id="bill_intro_date" align="center" class="textcenter"><br/>August 11, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr/><br clear="all"/><div id="title"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-size:0.9em;"> Relative to the County Welfare Directors Association of California’s Centennial Anniversary. </span></div><br clear="all"/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><h2>LEGISLATIVE COUNSEL'S DIGEST</h2></div><br/><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0"><span id="subject">SR 139, as introduced, Becker.
                          </span></div><div><span id="digesttext"/></div><span class="hidden"><h2>Digest Key</h2></span></div><hr/><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Text</h2></span><span class="Resolution" title="source: /caml:MeasureDoc/caml:Resolution&#xA;    "><span class="Whereas" id="id_E8D54094-878C-47B1-B19A-F6127245AA33"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The County Welfare Directors Association of California was first established in 1926 as the Association of California’s Executives of Public Welfare at the California Conference of Social Work; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_DDA5887D-7F8B-4D2F-B85E-A70BF7103BCF"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, In 1943, the organization became known as the County Welfare Directors Association; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_C209BF67-5DB8-4CF0-A721-E857576AFF5E"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The County Welfare Directors Association, known as CWDA, has, for 100 years, represented county human services agencies throughout California; and </div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_C81400C2-0445-4A6E-AAD0-02AE700A74BF"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA has worked at the local, state, and federal level advocating for the social safety net and the Californians served by its programs; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_C7A69D40-60FE-4888-8128-74E716AC5417"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA has, since its inception, worked closely with the State Department of Social Services on developing policies and regulations, including creating formal meetings beginning in 1944; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_1EC6BCBA-0528-42F0-BF1F-ACEE88A2EC5A"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA has played an integral role in the development and implementation of major policy initiatives to serve the people of California; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_483E0611-49A4-462B-9727-EF532B357E52"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, In 1998, CWDA helped create the statewide Adult Protective Services Program to protect elderly and dependent adults from abuse and neglect; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_9D22C34B-69E1-4345-9E24-756CD1DCFC39"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, In 2005, CWDA led the effort to protect elderly and dependent adults from financial exploitation by making banks and other financial institutions mandated reporters for elder abuse; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_39323982-CFF9-4B00-8C88-A40B48D97573"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA has a long history of advocating for and implementing welfare reform programs to better serve the poor and low-income families of California; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_95197002-3955-4ED5-93B3-7FB4D40DE1D8"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, In 1997, CWDA helped create the CalWORKs program in response to federal welfare reform; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_E0D03694-B102-4678-AE4B-DF5E45F9DC66"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA continues today as part of the Reimagine CalWORKs coalition to continue to reform and improve the CalWORKs program to benefit California’s families and children; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_C6232569-A8C7-4E4F-853D-B89E22DDEE2C"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA, representing child welfare agencies in California, has long advocated for the protection of children in the foster care system; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_066C044F-6C90-4E4E-AF67-F1D1BC71FEC1"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, In 2010, CWDA cosponsored legislation that expanded foster care from 18 years of age to 21 years of age so that young adults in the foster care system would have access to housing, education, and employment supports to improve their outcomes as they moved into adulthood; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_981297A7-C545-4C8A-A7E3-67927CC2B03D"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA continues to advocate for the betterment of California’s foster care system to ensure that foster children are given the tools they need to heal from trauma and thrive; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_40334C17-5EB6-4B1F-B8AE-B2E16E4D57F2"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA also continues to advance policies, practices, and funding to help prevent foster care entry and reduce disparities and disproportionality in the child welfare system; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_F27084F7-A237-44B8-B152-77269DDE7698"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA played an integral role in implementing the federal Affordable Care Act in 2013, and ensured that millions of new clients could enroll and access health care through the state Medi-Cal program; and </div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_C6E8B0EE-2A68-44D0-B248-210EDFE4927D"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, CWDA continues to advocate for Californians to have access to Medi-Cal and affordable health care and food assistance despite the attack on those programs by federal House Resolution 1 through investment in county enrollment and administration; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_2B8DD6B8-49AE-45F4-8879-B5C7DD0183F7"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, For 100 years, CWDA has advocated for the welfare of all Californians and will continue to advocate for and shape human services policies for many more years to come; now, therefore, be it</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_4FDBC164-A4AA-4454-A822-6C1367FF5BF3"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved by the Senate of the State of California, That the Senate honors the California Welfare Directors Association for its Centennial Anniversary; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_29E77C9C-8FB8-4B5A-A74F-544535209C0B"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Secretary of the Senate transmit copies of this resolution to the author for appropriate distribution.</div></span></span></div></body></html>
